Subject: [PATCH 08607/11362] Add conditional think-arm fallback on total
 induction failure (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6243)

Operator-directed follow-up to REQ-ARC-WMTE-6242's per-game breakdown: sp80's
no_think arm failed to produce any parseable engine while think scored 1.0 on
the same transitions; cd82/ls20/sk48 show the mirror failure. Neither "always
run both" (2b, still locked) nor "prefer think generally" (no such edge found)
fits -- the narrower fix is: if the currently-configured arm produces no
engine at all (heldout_accuracy is None), retry once with the other arm.
Excludes the 11/13 floor-tie games where retrying can't help.

Direction reads e3.induce_think_on() at call time rather than hardcoding a
side, since the live default is already think=1 (2026-08-08 operator flip) --
a hardcoded no_think-first fallback would have been a live no-op.

E3AgentPolicy._execute_bounded_llm_reinduction_with_arm_fallback wraps both
_induce_and_plan call sites (level_up_reinduction, stall-path). Env override
restored in a finally block -- the exact leak class REQ-6242's confound-fix
finding was about. Default OFF pending a live-path A/B, same standing
convention as every other lever in this plan.

Also resolved by reading the code rather than building infra: gemma-4's
think/no_think split is a prompt choice against the same running server
(/no_think is inert on gemma-4), not a model-load/restart difference, so the
sequential retry already has no teardown cost -- the L4x4 dual-preload idea
that prompted the question is better scoped as a separate concurrent-racing
lever (cuts wall-clock, not setup cost), noted but not built.

8 new tests, 59-test collateral sweep passes unchanged. 12 artifacts'
freshness acknowledgements updated (1 second-order cascade) for the touched
arc_competition_agent.py dependency, all verified-inert -- their own
generating scripts never set CARNOT_ARC_THINK_ARM_FALLBACK.
